# pstack — Jobs protocol

pstack is the site’s agent protocol and Cursor IDE model routing. Roles: How (ownership), Act (implement Jobs path only), Critic (verify-readyforrobots). It is not a customer chatbot and not the job matcher.

Hermes is retired. Do not spawn Hermes for FIND or Jobs. Do not follow `docs/hermes_intelligence_bridge.md` as production. Product loop is robot URL on `/` → Job Cards. FIND is `POST /api/robot-job-match` (`app/services/robot_job_capability_match.py`).

Checked-in runtime: `readyforrobots-new/client/src/lib/pstackSite.ts`, `app/services/pstack_protocol.py`, Jobs chrome `JobsPstackProtocol`. No npm pstack package. No Vercel AI Gateway.

## Before Jobs UI or API edits

Use `how` for ownership and layering. Do not invent a second matcher. CRM copilot (`docs/agent-spec.md`) is pstack Act, not Hermes.

## After Jobs UI copy

Run `unslop` on user-visible strings.

## PRs that change Jobs

If the diff touches `readyforrobots-new/` or the matcher, route through `.cursor/skills/verify-readyforrobots/SKILL.md`. FIND is `/`. Critic is pstack. Do not smoke `/experiment` as FIND.

## Harness roster → pstack roles

- Orchestrator = parent
- ProductSurface = frontend / Act
- LeadQuality = critics on names
- Deploy = Critic / verify-readyforrobots

Do not invent a Hermes pstack role. Do not use Vercel AI Gateway. Do not remove the CRM signup wall.
